# {{GuideName}} — Agent Skill

Install this published GuideAnts guide as an Agent Skill. It works with any agent
that supports the Agent Skills format (Claude Code, Cursor, and others).

## Install

Unzip into your agent's skills directory:

| Agent | Personal | Project |
|-------|----------|---------|
| Claude Code | `~/.claude/skills/{{SkillDirectoryName}}/` | `.claude/skills/{{SkillDirectoryName}}/` |
| Cursor | `~/.cursor/skills/{{SkillDirectoryName}}/` | `.cursor/skills/{{SkillDirectoryName}}/` |

## Configure

Edit `.env` (it is pre-filled when downloaded during an active API key session):

```
GUIDEANTS_API_BASE={{ApiBaseUrl}}
GUIDEANTS_PUB_ID={{PubId}}
GUIDEANTS_API_KEY=<your gak_ key>
```

Optional: set `GUIDEANTS_SAVE_DIR` to choose where deliverables are saved by
default when a command runs without `--save-dir`.

## Verify

```bash
cd {{SkillDirectoryName}}
python scripts/guideants_mcp.py doctor
```

Requires Python 3.8+ and nothing else — no curl, no bash, no third-party
packages. `python3` works too.

## Use

Invoke `/{{SkillName}}` (Claude Code or Cursor) or let the agent auto-load the
skill when a request matches its description.

## Security

- **Do not commit `.env` or this folder to git** — it contains your API key.
- The skill never prints the API key. If you rotate the key, update `.env` or
  re-download the skill pack.
